# calibration_dca.R is authored and run on Windows and is checked in with CRLF.
# Without this, line endings depend on each checkout's core.autocrlf: a clone on
# Linux can normalise it to LF, and an edit committed from Linux drops the CRLF
# for everyone. Pin it so the file on disk matches the file in the tree.
#
# R itself tolerates either ending. What it does not tolerate is a UTF-8 BOM on
# line 1, where the parse error looks like an empty file rather than an encoding
# problem — see analysis/README.md for the check.
*.R text eol=crlf

# Python stays LF everywhere, which is what every tool in this repo expects.
*.py text eol=lf
